Type: Package
Package: Rootopia
Title: Depth-Resolved Root Analysis and Trait Extraction from Minirhizotron
    and Flatbed Scanner Images
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Johannes",
             family = "Cunow",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "johannes.cunow@gmail.com",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4830-1162")))
Maintainer: Johannes Cunow <johannes.cunow@gmail.com>
Description: Extracts root traits from flatbed scanner images and from
    minirhizotron image sequences. Images are loaded, cleaned, thresholded and
    skeletonized, and traits are derived per image or summarized over depth
    intervals: root length, root diameter, branching points, root tips,
    branch and root order, turnover between sessions, and soil color and
    texture descriptors. For minirhizotron tubes, depth is resolved with a
    sinusoidal depth map built from tube diameter, insertion angle and
    resolution, and rotational bias along the tube axis can be quantified.
    Overlapping scans of one tube can be stitched into a single mosaic, and a
    batch wrapper runs the whole profile analysis over a directory of images.
    Minirhizotron scans must be segmented beforehand (e.g. with 'RootDetector'
    or 'RootPainter').
